    "title": "'Woodstock,' beloved Oakland-Alameda water shuttle, is back in service - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Alex Baker ,\n9 hours ago\n( KRON ) -- \"Woodstock,\" the beloved, bright yellow ferry that shuttles people back and forth between Alameda and Oakland's Jack London Square, was back in service Wednesday. The 31-passenger vessel had been out of service since Aug. 5 due to engine issues.\nLast week, the San Francisco Bay Ferry said that ferry would be out of service until at least Friday, Aug. 21. That deadline came and went, and the former Niagara Falls tour boat was still out of action.\nBeloved California brewery Stone Brewing shutting down, laying off hundreds However, as of Wednesday at 7:20 a.m., Woodstock had resumed service, according to the SF Bay Ferry website.\nWoodstock, the vessel to become the Alameda-Oakland water shuttle, arrives at Jack London Square to begin final modifications. The vessel is scheduled to take passengers from Bohol Circle Park across to Oakland at the end of June. Woodstock runs daily from 7:20 a.m. until 7:48 p.m. from Monday through Friday and from 7:20 a.m. through 9:43 p.m. on Saturday and Sunday. The pontoon boat ferries passengers back and forth between Jack London Square and Alameda Landing, near Target on 5th Street.\nRecently, the pilot ferry program, which was introduced in 2024, was extended through 2028.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed.\nFor the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to KRON4.\n1",
    "summary": "Beloved California brewery Stone Brewing shutting down, laying off hundreds However, as of Wednesday at 7:20 a.m., Woodstock had resumed service, according to the SF Bay Ferry website. Woodstock, the vessel to become the Alameda-Oakland water shuttle, arrives at Jack London Square to begin final modifications. The vessel is scheduled to take passengers from Bohol Circle Park across to Oakland at the end of June. Woodstock runs daily from 7:20 a.m. until 7:48 p.m. from Monday through Friday and from 7:20 a.m. through 9:43 p.m. on Saturday and Sunday.",
